      "event": {
        "id": 0,
        "job": 1,
        "text": "The riverbank in the early morning is always very quiet. The thin mist slowly spreads across the water’s surface. The old people on the shore are practicing Tai Chi. The small stalls that sell breakfast have just set up their stoves. The water flow under the bridge is slow. A few white egrets stand still on the shallow waters, staring at the small fish in the water. Occasionally, bicycles pass by on the stone-paved path. The bells ring loudly, but soon they disappear behind the street corners.",
        "type": "translated"
      },
      "t_ms": 2790
    },
    {
      "event": {
        "id": 1,
        "job": 1,
        "text": "This river was once forgotten due to its pollution. Over twenty years ago, the local residents organized themselves to clean up the riverbank, planting willows and reeds. Later, the government also joined in, building paths and small parks along the river. Now, on weekends, children chase each other by the water, while young people use their cameras to find the right angle to take pictures. The river has once again become one of the most popular public spaces here. People often say that whether a city is livable depends on its rivers.",
        "type": "translated"
      },
      "t_ms": 5313
    },
